{"id":"rdb-cf94d8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Validate concurrent embedded and server sessions","description":"Add integration tests that exercise concurrent access patterns:\n\n- Embedded session writing while the MySQL server is running against the same catalog\n- Multiple embedded sessions in parallel goroutines\n- Worktree switching mid-session (open engine on one worktree, switch, verify isolation)\n\nThese are the \"validate concurrent embedded/server use\" and \"worktree switching\" items from the original M5 plan. The engine already supports these patterns but they lack dedicated test coverage.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a0","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:21:39.627372Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-4a685e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Resilience tests: read-only clones, missing executables, network and hook failures","description":"Add integration tests for degraded/edge-case environments:\n\n- Read-only clone (no push access): verify reads work, writes to local journal work, sync fails gracefully\n- Missing `git` executable: verify clear error at engine.Open\n- Network failure mid-sync: verify partial sync does not corrupt local state\n- Hook failures: verify hook errors are surfaced, not silently swallowed\n\nCovers the \"validate read-only clones, missing executables, hook failures, network failures, and partial synchronization\" item from M5.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a1","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:21:43.482106Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-33512b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Workflow and operations documentation","description":"Write user-facing documentation covering the full operational workflow:\n\n- Enable / embedded use / server start\n- Status / diff / data commit lifecycle\n- Journal backup and recovery procedures\n- Sync workflow and conflict resolution\n- Hook policy (what hooks exist, when they fire, how to configure)\n\nThe existing docs cover individual subsystems (sql-m2, sync-m3, merge-m4, working-state) but there is no unified \"how to use RepoDB\" guide that walks through the full lifecycle.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a2","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:21:48.455626Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e45ce6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Expand supported SQL types and collations","description":"Broaden the set of SQL types and collation support beyond the current minimal set. Candidates:\n\n- DATE, TIME, DATETIME, TIMESTAMP\n- DECIMAL / NUMERIC\n- ENUM\n- JSON (native type, not just TEXT)\n- Collation-aware string comparisons (at least utf8mb4_general_ci)\n\nEach type needs: DDL support, storage round-trip, comparison/ordering, and behavioral tests. Scope to the types that real consumers (nate, embedded tools) actually need — don't chase MySQL parity for its own sake.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a3","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:21:53.440747Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-4dd186","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"CHECK and UNIQUE constraints","description":"Support constraint enforcement beyond PRIMARY KEY:\n\n- `UNIQUE` constraints (single-column and composite)\n- `CHECK` constraints\n- `NOT NULL` on non-PK columns (verify current behavior, add tests if already working)\n- `DEFAULT` values\n\nConstraints must be enforced on INSERT and UPDATE, persisted in the catalog, and round-tripped through sync/merge. Constraint violations should return clear SQL errors.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a4","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:21:56.721318Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-686c51","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MySQL driver and ORM behavioral compatibility tests","description":"Build a test suite that connects to the RepoDB MySQL server using standard MySQL drivers and ORMs to identify compatibility gaps:\n\n- Go `database/sql` with `go-sql-driver/mysql`\n- Basic ORM (e.g. sqlx or GORM) connection and CRUD\n- Prepared statements, transactions, error codes\n- Information schema queries that tools commonly run\n\nGoal is to document what works and what doesn't, not to fix everything — the fixes become their own issues.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a5","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:06.585091Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-db5459","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Workload profiling: append-heavy and mutable-data benchmarks","description":"Measure performance for the two primary consumer workload shapes:\n\n- **Append-heavy** (agent traces / event logs): high-volume inserts, range scans by time, rare updates\n- **Mutable** (issue tracker / board): frequent updates to existing rows, point reads, filtered queries\n\nMeasure: commit latency, query latency, memory use, repository size growth over time, and sync cost at various data volumes (1k, 10k, 100k rows).\n\nResults inform where optimization effort should go (tree mutation, caching, compaction).","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a6","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:12.049443Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-16df08","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Corruption detection and recovery","description":"Handle corrupted or inconsistent state gracefully:\n\n- Detect corrupted journal entries (truncated writes, bad checksums) and skip/report them\n- Detect catalog/tree inconsistencies on open and report clearly\n- `repodb fsck` command to validate storage integrity\n- Recovery path: rebuild from last known-good Git snapshot when journal is corrupt\n\nCurrently a corrupted journal or tree can cause panics or silent data loss.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a7","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:15.753795Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-8ecac5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fuzz testing for SQL bind and storage paths","description":"Add Go native fuzz tests (`testing.F`) for high-risk input paths:\n\n- `bind()` / `sqlLiteral()` — arbitrary string values with special characters\n- Journal record encoding/decoding — arbitrary row data\n- Prolly tree key encoding — arbitrary typed values\n\nGoal is to catch edge cases like the backslash bug (rdb-1ed603) before they reach users.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a8","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:19.897376Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-515fae","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Journal retention and compaction","description":"The journal grows without bound today. Add a compaction strategy:\n\n- After a successful checkpoint, truncate or archive journal entries that are now materialized in Git\n- Configurable retention policy (keep N checkpoints of journal history, or time-based)\n- `repodb compact` command for manual compaction\n- Measure repository size savings\n\nWithout this, long-running embedded tools will accumulate unbounded journal data.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a9","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:23.529384Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-5720c1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Server authentication and TLS","description":"The MySQL server currently accepts any connection with no authentication and no encryption. For standalone network use, add:\n\n- Username/password authentication (MySQL native auth protocol)\n- TLS support (certificate configuration)\n- Bind address configuration (currently hardcoded to 127.0.0.1, which is safe for local use)\n\nThis is only needed when the server is exposed beyond localhost. Local-only and embedded use are unaffected.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aA","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:26.915909Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a65375","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Secondary indexes","description":"Add support for secondary indexes to accelerate non-PK lookups.\n\nThis is a cross-cutting feature touching storage, DDL, query execution, merge, and sync:\n\n- `CREATE INDEX` / `DROP INDEX` DDL\n- Index storage as separate prolly trees alongside the table tree\n- Query planner integration: use index for equality and range predicates\n- Index maintenance on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE\n- Index merge during three-way reconciliation\n- Index rebuild / consistency check\n\nBreak into sub-issues once the design is clearer:\n1. Index storage format and DDL\n2. Index maintenance on writes\n3. Query planner index selection\n4. Index merge during sync","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":8,"sort_order":"aB","labels":["feature","epic"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:22:39.187757Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
