{"id":"rdb-68106e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c96c8654-3096-4400-809f-aca0c4d052e3","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Changes\n\n**`engine/catalog.go`** — 5 edits:\n\n1. **`columnDisk` struct**: Added `Default`, `DefaultLit`, `DefaultParen` fields (all `json:\",omitempty\"` for backward compat)\n2. **`encodeSchema`**: Serializes `col.Default.String()` and the `IsLiteral()`/`IsParenthesized()` flags\n3. **`decodeSchema`**: Reconstructs defaults via `sql.NewUnresolvedColumnDefaultValue()` with the stored flags — go-mysql-server's analyzer resolves the expression at query time\n4. **`validateSchema`**: Removed `col.Default != nil` from the rejection (keeps `AutoIncrement` and `Generated` blocked)\n5. **`AddColumn`**: NOT NULL rejection now only fires when `column.Default == nil` — go-mysql-server's `addColumnIter.UpdateRowsWithDefaults()` handles backfilling via our existing `UpdatableTable` interface\n\n**`engine/engine_test.go`** — 8 new tests:\n\n- `TestCreateTableWithDefaultLiteral` — literal string and int defaults on INSERT with omitted columns\n- `TestCreateTableWithDefaultExpression` — parenthesized expression default `(1 + 1)`\n- `TestInsertExplicitDefaultKeyword` — `INSERT INTO t VALUES (1, DEFAULT)`\n- `TestAlterTableAddNotNullWithDefault` — backfills existing rows with the default value\n- `TestAlterTableAddNotNullNoDefaultStillRejected` — regression guard\n- `TestDefaultPersistsThroughReopen` — working-state persistence round-trip\n- `TestDefaultPersistsNativeGit` — native git persistence round-trip\n\n### Key design decision\n\nNo backfill logic in RepoDB's `AddColumn`. go-mysql-server's `addColumnIter` calls `AddColumn` (which inserts `nil` placeholders), then calls `UpdateRowsWithDefaults` which iterates via our `Updater()` to apply the resolved default to each row. This keeps RepoDB's integrator thin.\n\n### All tests pass\n\nFull suite: `go test ./...` — all packages green."},"created_at":"2026-09-14T09:28:42.572191Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
