{"id":"rdb-4dd186","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"CHECK constraints","description":"Support CHECK constraint enforcement:\\n\\n- `CHECK` constraints in CREATE TABLE and ALTER TABLE\\n- Persist check definitions in the catalog\\n- Round-trip through sync/merge\\n- Constraint violations return clear SQL errors\\n- Verify and test NOT NULL enforcement on non-PK columns (already handled by go-mysql-server)\\n\\ngo-mysql-server handles all expression parsing, validation, and enforcement during INSERT/UPDATE. RepoDB only needs to store and return `CheckDefinition` objects.\\n\\nDEFAULT values were shipped in rdb-68106e. UNIQUE constraints are tracked separately and depend on secondary index infrastructure.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-14T10:11:18.391786Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"UNIQUE constraints","description":"Support UNIQUE constraints (single-column and composite):\\n\\n- `UNIQUE` in CREATE TABLE and ALTER TABLE ADD INDEX/CONSTRAINT\\n- Enforce uniqueness on INSERT and UPDATE\\n- Persist index metadata in the catalog\\n- Return unique indexes from `GetIndexes()`\\n- Implement `sql.IndexAlterableTable` (CreateIndex, DropIndex, RenameIndex)\\n\\nUniqueness enforcement requires proper secondary index data structures — brute-force scanning is not viable for performance. This depends on the secondary indexes epic (rdb-a65375).","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aD","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-a1f9d1","target_id":"rdb-a65375","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T10:11:21.736035Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
