{"id":"rdb-738fd0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Prolly tree prefix iteration","description":"Add prefix-based iteration to the prolly tree so callers can efficiently find all entries whose key starts with a given prefix.\n\nThe tree currently supports:\n- `Get(key)` — single point lookup\n- `Iterator()` — full scan from start\n- `Entries()` — materialize all entries\n\nNon-unique secondary indexes store one entry per (indexed-columns, PK) pair. Looking up all rows matching a set of indexed column values requires scanning all entries with a common key prefix. Without prefix iteration, the only option is a full table scan.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- `IteratorFrom(ctx, startKey)` — positions the iterator at the first entry \u003e= startKey\n- Callers combine this with a prefix check to implement prefix scans\n- Tests for seeking into various positions, prefix boundaries, empty trees","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-a65375","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a2","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:45:38.870185Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-4bdf5d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Non-unique secondary index support","description":"Generalize the UNIQUE constraint index infrastructure to support non-unique secondary indexes.\n\nThe UNIQUE constraint work (rdb-a1f9d1) built the core index machinery: prolly tree storage, key encoding, index maintenance on writes, DDL, merge rebuild. This issue extends it to non-unique indexes.\n\n**Key changes:**\n- Remove `CREATE INDEX` rejection of non-unique indexes (catalog.go:727)\n- Non-unique key encoding: always append PK as disambiguator (not just for NULLs)\n- Generalize `uniqueIndex` type → `secondaryIndex` with `IsUnique()` returning `def.Unique`\n- `Insert`: maintain non-unique indexes (skip uniqueness check, still add index edit)\n- `lookupSecondaryPartitions`: prefix scan via `IteratorFrom` to find all matching PKs\n- `LookupPartitions`: handle the new `secondaryIndex` type\n- `GetIndexes`: return correct type based on `def.Unique`\n\n**Depends on:** Prolly tree prefix iteration","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-a65375","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a3","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:45:46.289075Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
