{"id":"rdb-4bdf5d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0830251f-b79b-4975-be98-951019dd08e5","text":"Implementation complete. Changes across 3 files, 11 new tests.\n\n**`engine/catalog.go`:**\n\n- `encodeIndexKey` — added `unique bool` parameter. When `!unique`, PK is always appended as disambiguator (not just for NULLs). All 11 call sites updated.\n- `CreateIndex` — removed `!def.IsUnique()` rejection gate. Non-unique indexes created with `Unique: false`. Uniqueness scan only runs for unique indexes.\n- Renamed `uniqueIndex` → `secondaryIndex`. `IsUnique()` now returns `def.Unique` instead of hardcoded `true`.\n- `GetIndexes` — returns `secondaryIndex` for all non-primary indexes.\n- `Insert` — removed `if !idx.Unique { continue }`. All indexes now maintained; uniqueness check gated on `idx.Unique`.\n- `Delete` / `Update` — `encodeIndexKey` calls updated with `idx.Unique` parameter.\n- `LookupPartitions` — dispatches `secondaryIndex` to `lookupUniquePartitions` (when unique) or new `lookupSecondaryPartitions`.\n- New `lookupSecondaryPartitions` — encodes column values as prefix, calls `resolveIndexToPKs` to find all matching rows.\n- New `resolveIndexToPKs` — prefix scan via `IteratorFrom` on persisted tree, merges with pending edits.\n\n**`engine/merge.go`:**\n- `rebuildIndexesFromTree` — `encodeIndexKey` call updated with `idx.Unique`.\n\n**11 new tests:**\n1. `TestSecondaryIndexDDL` — CREATE INDEX + query\n2. `TestSecondaryIndexDuplicatesAllowed` — multiple rows with same value\n3. `TestSecondaryIndexMaintainedOnDelete` — index updated on DELETE\n4. `TestSecondaryIndexMaintainedOnUpdate` — index updated on UPDATE\n5. `TestSecondaryIndexNullValues` — NULLs handled correctly\n6. `TestSecondaryIndexComposite` — multi-column index\n7. `TestSecondaryIndexPersistence` — survives close/reopen\n8. `TestSecondaryIndexDropIndex` — DROP INDEX works\n9. `TestSecondaryIndexAlterTableAdd` — CREATE INDEX on existing table\n10. `TestSecondaryIndexNativeGit` — native-git persistence mode\n11. `TestSecondaryIndexCoexistsWithUnique` — unique + non-unique on same table\n\nFull suite passes (23 unique + 11 secondary = 34 index tests total)."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T16:21:37.657363Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
