{"id":"rdb-bc2820","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-224aeadc-e9a3-41e3-beb4-7cd4e4ea14f8","text":"Implementation complete. Changes:\n\n**`integration/integration.go`** — Added `resolveRemote()` helper that bundles `CLI.Discover()` + remote resolution. When the explicit remote is empty, it reads `repodb.remote` from local Git config. Returns `ErrRemoteRequired` if both the flag and config are absent (or config is ambiguous). Updated `Sync()` to use it.\n\n**`integration/conflicts.go`** — Updated `Conflicts()` and `Resolve()` to use `resolveRemote()` instead of `requireRemote()` + separate `repository.Discover()`.\n\n**`integration/integration_test.go`** — Added `TestResolveRemoteFromConfig` covering: config fallback for sync, explicit flag override, conflicts fallback, missing config error, and enable still requiring explicit remote.\n\n`Enable()` is unchanged — it continues to require an explicit `--remote` since it's the command that sets the config value. No CLI (`main.go`) changes needed — the empty-string default from the flag naturally flows into `resolveRemote`.\n\nAll tests pass (full suite, no regressions)."},"created_at":"2026-09-17T14:31:45.460065Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
