{"id":"rdb-52da05","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Windows support: cross-platform file locks via gofrs/flock","description":"RepoDB does not compile for `GOOS=windows` because the working-state and publish locks call `unix.Flock` directly (`common/repository/working.go`, `common/repository/repository.go`).\n\nBoth locks already use a dedicated lock file (`locks/working.lock`, `locks/publish.lock`) polled with a non-blocking exclusive lock — the same pattern `gofrs/flock`'s `TryLockContext(ctx, retryDelay)` implements on Unix (flock(2)) and Windows (LockFileEx). Swap both sites to gofrs/flock; the design doesn't change.\n\n- [ ] Replace `unix.Flock` in both lock sites with `flock.TryLockContext`\n- [ ] Remove remaining non-portable `x/sys/unix` usage blocking `GOOS=windows go build ./...` / `go vet ./...`\n- [ ] Tests pass on darwin; Windows cross-compile + vet clean","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:03:24.524283Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
