{"id":"rdb-1e11b2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Data-ref pushes run the host repo's pre-push hook, causing infinite recursion","description":"`PushRef` and `PushCommit` in `common/git/git.go` publish RepoDB data with a plain `git push`, which runs the host repository's `pre-push` hook. A tool that syncs RepoDB from a pre-push hook (e.g. nate's hook running `nate sync`) recurses without limit: each sync pushes, the push runs the hook, the hook syncs again. In testing one push produced 11 nested sync processes in ~6s and the data ref never reached the remote.\n\nRepoDB's data ref is internal bookkeeping; user push hooks (linters, test gates, sync tools) should never run against it.\n\n**Affected code (9bdef12)**\n- `common/git/git.go:171` — `PushRef`\n- `common/git/git.go:181` — `PushCommit`\n\n**Fix:** pass `--no-verify` on both data-ref pushes, and on any other push RepoDB makes on its own behalf. Fetches don't run client-side hooks.\n\nDownstream tracking: nate `nate-d00caf`.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:53:59.215042Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
