{"id":"rdb-d3c729","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Lower go directive to 1.25 (x/sys v0.47.0, x/term v0.45.0)","description":"RepoDB declares `go 1.27` in go.mod, a leftover from the initial scaffold that recorded the local toolchain. As a library it should declare the lowest Go version it actually needs, so consumers on older toolchains can use it.\n\nThe real floor is 1.25: `gofrs/flock v0.13.1` requires 1.25. Only `golang.org/x/sys v0.48.0` and `golang.org/x/term v0.46.0` require 1.26; their predecessors (x/sys v0.47.0, x/term v0.45.0) require 1.25.\n\nInvestigation (scratch copy): build, vet (incl. `stdversion` and GOOS=windows) and full test suite pass at `go 1.25.0`. govulncheck reports no vulnerabilities in x/sys v0.47.0 / x/term v0.45.0; the diffs to the newer versions contain no security fixes and touch nothing RepoDB uses (`term.IsTerminal`, `unix.Getrusage`, `windows.ERROR_*`).\n\n- [ ] go.mod: `go 1.25.0`, x/sys v0.47.0, x/term v0.45.0\n- [ ] README: update Go version requirement (and stale \"requires POSIX file locking\" note)","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a0","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T08:53:21.757693Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d3c729","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"RepoDB declares `go 1.27` in go.mod, a leftover from the initial scaffold that recorded the local toolchain. As a library it should declare the lowest Go version it actually needs, so consumers on older toolchains can use it.\n\nThe real floor is 1.25: `gofrs/flock v0.13.1` requires 1.25. Only `golang.org/x/sys v0.48.0` and `golang.org/x/term v0.46.0` require 1.26; their predecessors (x/sys v0.47.0, x/term v0.45.0) require 1.25.\n\nInvestigation (scratch copy): build, vet (incl. `stdversion` and GOOS=windows) and full test suite pass at `go 1.25.0`. govulncheck reports no vulnerabilities in x/sys v0.47.0 / x/term v0.45.0; the diffs to the newer versions contain no security fixes and touch nothing RepoDB uses (`term.IsTerminal`, `unix.Getrusage`, `windows.ERROR_*`).\n\n- [ ] go.mod: `go 1.25.0`, x/sys v0.47.0, x/term v0.45.0\n- [ ] README: update Go version requirement","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T08:53:38.464598Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d86f52","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Docs still say POSIX file locking is required after Windows support","description":"Since rdb-52da05 (cross-platform file locks via gofrs/flock), RepoDB builds and locks on Windows too, but the docs still describe the lock as POSIX-only:\n\n- `README.md` Installation: \"The current implementation requires POSIX file locking\"\n- `docs/storage-format.md:52`: \"The lock is an advisory POSIX file lock shared by linked worktrees and processes.\"\n- `docs/storage-format.md:77`: \"implementation requires POSIX `flock`\"\n\nUpdate these to describe the cross-platform lock (flock on Unix, LockFileEx on Windows) and the supported/tested platforms.\n\nFound while working on rdb-d3c729.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a8","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-d86f52","target_id":"rdb-d3c729","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","docs"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T08:53:38.485655Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
