{"id":"rdb-3745e6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`repodb commit` drops journal row edits (data loss)","description":"Found while cross-version testing rdb-855cac; reproduces on `main` (de20d6a) and is unrelated to the go-mysql-server upgrade.\n\n## Repro\n\n```sh\nrepodb init .\nrepodb start --persistence journal --addr 127.0.0.1:34875 \u0026\nrepodb sql --addr 127.0.0.1:34875 --database repodb \"CREATE TABLE p (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, label VARCHAR(20))\"\nrepodb sql --addr 127.0.0.1:34875 --database repodb \"INSERT INTO p VALUES (1,'a'),(2,'b')\"\n# SELECT COUNT(*) -\u003e 2\nkill %1\nrepodb commit -m checkpoint   # succeeds, status goes dirty -\u003e clean\nrepodb start --persistence journal ... ; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM p  -\u003e 0\n```\n\nThe table survives, but every row is lost.\n\n## Cause\n\n`cmd/repodb/main.go:107-108` calls `repository.WorkingState.Checkpoint` directly. That publishes the working snapshot's objects but ignores `snapshot.PendingEdits()`, the typed row edits the journal records. `engine.Engine.Checkpoint` handles these via `checkpointTypedEdits`; the CLI bypasses it. It then marks the working state clean, so the edits are gone. The error from `OpenWorkingState` is also discarded.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nHave the CLI checkpoint through `engine.NewWithOptions(repo, Options{Persistence: journal}).Checkpoint`, or make `WorkingState.Checkpoint` refuse or handle pending typed edits so no caller can drop them. Add a CLI-level regression test.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-3745e6","target_id":"rdb-855cac","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:37:14.022908Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e472aa","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Journal writes skip secondary indexes on tables with snapshot rows (UNIQUE violated)","description":"Found while cross-version testing rdb-855cac; reproduces on `main` (de20d6a) with plain BIGINT columns and is unrelated to the go-mysql-server upgrade.\n\n## Repro\n\n```sh\nrepodb start --persistence native-git ...\n  CREATE TABLE t (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, v BIGINT, UNIQUE KEY v_idx (v));\n  INSERT INTO t VALUES (1, 10);\n# stop, then\nrepodb start --persistence journal ...\n  INSERT INTO t VALUES (2, 20);\n  SELECT id FROM t WHERE v = 20;   -- returns nothing (expected 2), even before restart\n  INSERT INTO t VALUES (3, 20);    -- accepted: UNIQUE constraint violated\n  SELECT * FROM t;                 -- (1,10) (2,20) (3,20)\n```\n\nLookups through the index for the snapshot row (`v = 10`) still work. If the table is empty when journal writes begin (created in either mode), the index is maintained correctly and uniqueness is enforced.\n\n## Impact\n\nWrong query results for index-planned queries, and UNIQUE constraints silently violated. The corrupt state persists across restarts and presumably into checkpoints.\n\n## Notes\n\nLikely in how journal-mode typed row edits are applied to secondary-index trees when the base snapshot already has an index tree (`tableState.idxEdits` / `ensureIndexEdits` in `engine/catalog.go`), but not yet investigated. Add a regression test covering snapshot rows, then journal insert/update/delete, with both lookup and uniqueness checks.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a1","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-e472aa","target_id":"rdb-855cac","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:39:17.64645Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-855cac","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:44:28.523971Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-6bf1cc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`repodb sql 'EXPLAIN ...'` fails: strconv.ParseUint parsing \"NULL\"","description":"Found while testing rdb-855cac; reproduces on `main` (de20d6a) and with the upgraded go-mysql-server.\n\n```sh\nrepodb sql --addr ... --database repodb \"EXPLAIN SELECT label FROM p WHERE amt = 1.5\"\nrepodb: strconv.ParseUint: parsing \"NULL\": invalid syntax\n```\n\nLikely the CLI client scanning an EXPLAIN result column that is NULL into an unsigned integer (MySQL-style EXPLAIN rows contain NULL `possible_keys`/`key_len`/etc.). Not investigated further.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a9","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-6bf1cc","target_id":"rdb-855cac","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:44:28.549939Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-855cac","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-455233f9-89ae-4783-b708-6168852414a6","text":"Implemented; spec updated to match (it grew during implementation).\n\n**Changes**\n- GMS → `v0.20.1-0.20260925233942-d8e4c765db15`, vitess and friends follow; go directive 1.26.2.\n- engine/: `*sql.Context` signature changes, `ConvertInRange`, `Function1.Fn`, `CoversColumns` (false), JSON ctx.\n- DECIMAL: GMS now uses `*apd.Decimal`. Storage encoding kept byte-identical (apd → shopspring `String()`); decode via apd. Embedded `Query` rows now carry `*apd.Decimal` formatted at column scale (MySQL-correct `0.10`); `TestDecimalRoundTrip` updated.\n- server: `Close` made idempotent; GMS's Close panics on a second call.\n- Makefile exports `GOFLAGS += -tags=gms_pure_go`; README documents Go 1.26 and the tag.\n- Security bumps beyond GMS: grpc v1.83.2 (v1.84.0 is still affected by GO-2026-6443), x/text v0.41.0, otel v1.44.0 via grpc.\n\n**Verification**\n- `make test` (incl. Windows cross build + vet), `go vet`, `go test -race` on repository/engine/integration: pass.\n- govulncheck: no vulnerabilities in any module.\n- Cross-version: DECIMAL PK/index data written by the old binary (native-git and journal) is readable, point- and index-lookupable, and uniqueness is enforced in the new binary.\n\n**Pre-existing bugs found (on main, unrelated to the upgrade)**\n- rdb-3745e6: `repodb commit` drops journal row edits (data loss).\n- rdb-e472aa: journal writes skip secondary indexes when the table has snapshot rows (UNIQUE violated).\n- rdb-6bf1cc: `repodb sql 'EXPLAIN …'` fails parsing NULL.\n\n`engine/performance.go` and `engine/working_test.go` are not gofmt-clean on main; left untouched."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:44:36.713406Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
