{"id":"rdb-3745e6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-52c2b7bf-5a3d-471b-a929-4a8fc641ff82","text":"Implemented per spec.\n\n- `cmd/repodb`: `commit` and the sync checkpoint prompt go through a new `checkpoint` helper (journal engine → `Checkpoint` → `Close`); `promptCheckpointIfDirty` no longer discards the `OpenWorkingState` error.\n- `WorkingState.Checkpoint` returns `ErrPendingRowEdits` (OutcomeRejected, nothing published) when typed row edits are pending.\n- `BenchmarkM43JournalCheckpoint` now uses `eng.Checkpoint`; it previously timed the row-dropping path.\n- Tests: `TestWorkingCheckpointRefusesPendingRowEdits` (engine) and `TestCommitKeepsJournalRows` (cmd/repodb, first test for that package). Against the pre-fix CLI, the new test fails with ErrPendingRowEdits.\n- The binary repro keeps both rows. `make test` and race (incl. cmd/repodb) pass.\n\nNot covered by an automated test: the sync prompt path (reads stdin and needs a remote); it shares the same helper.\nHeads-up: `docs/m4.3-bench.md` numbers for the journal checkpoint benchmark were measured on the dropping path and are likely optimistic."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:53:00.018295Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
